  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIn the [inner navigate event firing algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#inner-navigate-event-firing-algorithm), at the step of waiting for all of `promisesList`, in the event of a failure, the event's [interception state](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#concept-navigateevent-interception-state) will still be \"intercepted\". The steps in the rejection handler do not change the event state before calling the [finish event given false](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#navigateevent-finish) steps and the first assertion will then fail ([Assert](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#assert): event's [interception state](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#concept-navigateevent-interception-state) is not \"intercepted\" or \"finished\".). Either the state needs to be updated before doing this or the assertion should be skipped when finishing the event given `false`.",
